WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.500
 Hello, everyone. I've brought you all here today because I am proposing a problem that we need to address.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:27.500
 I believe that humans are important, and I think humans are valuable, and they do not deserve the treatment that our species has been giving them.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:46.200
 For example, a human was taken on board recently and done many experiments that were considered to be quite uncomfortable and possibly even painful to the human.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:01:04.080
 The human had exhibited signs of distress. There was squirming, there was squealing, there was face leaking, which is one of the most sure signs that a human is in great distress.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:17.380
 We were led to believe that humans were of less value because of the way they looked, because of where they came from, because of their intelligence level.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:28.140
 Well, I want to convince you today that humans are of much value and their lives are just as important as ours.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:44.180
 Why do we respect the Martians but we abduct and kill the earthlings? What's the difference between them besides their intelligence level?

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:56.540
 Just because a creature is not as intelligent as us doesn't mean that we have the right to capture, abuse, and kill them.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:17.500
 So, I have a list here today, to discuss the reasons why humans are cute, and they're sweet, and loving, and they have their own feelings and emotions.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:31.500
 Okay, may I read the list to you? Here is my supporting evidence that humans are worthy of our respect and maybe our love.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:42.560
 Humans say ouch whenever they have not been hurt, but just think that they might have been hurt, but aren't sure yet.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:49.340
 Humans collect shiny things to decorate their body and their nest with.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:57.620
 The shinier the better, although individual humans have their own unique styles and tastes.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:08.820
 Humans are not aquatic creatures, nor are they amphibious, but still they flock to bodies of water just to play in it.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.060
 They can't even hold their breath for that long, they just love to splash.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:25.340
 When the night falls and the sky becomes dark, humans become drowsy and begin to cocoon themselves in fluffy bedding.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.580
 Some humans spend time in each other's nests just for fun.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.980
 It's not their nest, they're just visiting.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:45.140
 Some humans use pigments and dyes to make their bodies flashy and colorful.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.560
 They even attach dangly bits to their cartilage membranes.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:55.600
 Shiny, as their preference is.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:03.000
 Humans are very clever and sometimes adopt species outside of their own into their family units.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:10.180
 They don't seem to notice the obvious differences, and often raise them alongside their own young.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:17.960
 If a human sees another creature in distress, they are commonly observed to try and help.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.540
 Even at their own risk, humans are very naturally compassionate creatures.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:32.980
 If a human hears in a particularly catchy sound or tune, they will often mimic it, even to the point of annoying themselves.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:41.560
 Sneezes are entirely involuntary and completely adorable, especially when the human in question becomes frustrated.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.400
 Humans love treats, some more than others.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:52.740
 Many humans will save these treats for a later date, especially when they are in need of comfort and reassurance.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.320
 For example, pickles, pop-tarts, etc.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.900
 They are learning to travel space.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:05.380
 They haven't gotten very far, but they're trying.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:12.420
 So far they've made it to the end of their yard, and they've found rocks.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:21.400
 This concludes my proposal for humans to be considered as a useful and important part of our solar system.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:27.020
 And I think we should consider them to be friends, not enemies.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:38.660
 And instead of experimenting on them, we should converse with them, learn their ways, and try to learn more about them in a more humane way.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:46.100
 My name is Faye. Thank you for listening. I hope you consider what I have said today. Goodbye.
